 "assumptions": {
  "reverse": "CCW and downhill reverse the corner order.",
  "ir_dr_flip": "IR and DR swap when the lap is reversed (an increasing-radius corner is a decreasing-radius corner in the other direction). HP, ES, CH, N90, CR, SW are treated as direction-symmetric. The sim has no left/right handedness, so CW vs CCW is order plus this IR/DR flip only.",
  "grade_source": "unapproved/arthur/mockups/districts/README.md Pass 2 (Austin 2026-11-13) and CHANGELOG 2026-11-13 Arthur: Touge climbs at 8.5% on the approach, crests in the hairpin (0% at ~75% of the arc), falls at 5% out of it, banks up to 6%. Street and Wangan stay flat. That pass was presentation-only (scoring/sim unchanged). There is no published sim rule for uphill vs downhill heat; the gravity tilt below is a PLACEHOLDER that reuses those grade percents.",
  "gravity": "On Touge only, after track_wear and before capacity calibration, multiply wear POW/HAN/EN then renormalise so the lap's total load is unchanged. Uphill (climbing the 8.5% approach, with 5% drops still in the profile): POW*(1+0.085), HAN*1, EN*(1-0.05). Downhill (reversed hairpin: 5% local climbs, 8.5% drops): POW*(1-0.05), HAN*1, EN*(1+0.085). Street and Wangan stay flat (multiplier 1). PLACEHOLDER pending Austin."
 },
 "sources": {
  "touge_layout": "T1_Akina_Switchbacks",
  "street_layouts": [
   "S1_Shibuya_Grid",
   "S3_Shinjuku_Underpass"
  ],
  "wangan_layouts": [
   "W1_Bayshore_Run",
   "W3_C1_Outer"
  ],
  "why": "T1 is the hairpin-heavy switchback stand-in (Touge signature corners HP/ES/DR). S1 is the Street grid (signature N90+CH); S3 is a second Street layout with more chicanes and mixed types. W1 is the open-highway Bayshore stand-in (signature SW/IR/CR); W3 is a second Wangan loop (adds an N90). CW/uphill = the authored tracks_v1.json order. Other stand-ins (T2-T5, S2/S4/S5, W2/W4/W5) are dropped for this study."
 }
}